[h1]Worker Optimizer[/h1]
[b]Auto-assign workers to suitable jobs with one click, or let a schedule handle it.[/b]

Match your residents' specialties to your settlement's needs, respect your priorities and keep enough workers available for construction.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Smart assignment:[/b] considers worker specialties, productivity and job requirements.
[*][b]Coverage first:[/b] prioritize minimum operating crews before filling extra workplaces.
[*][b]Your priorities:[/b] searchable building categories and individual building-type overrides.
[*][b]Builder reserve:[/b] choose how many eligible residents remain unassigned.
[*][b]Optional automation:[/b] run at day start or every 5, 10 or 15 real-time minutes.
[*][b]Clear logbook:[/b] timestamps, color-coded results, confirmed changes and reasons for unfilled workplaces.
[*][b]Responsive interface:[/b] General, Priorities and Logbook, supporting all 17 game languages.
[/list]

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[b]Recommended timing:[/b] For best results, run worker assignment calculations at night or just after a new day starts. Running them during the day may cause assignment errors.

Subscribe, wait for Steam to download the mod and restart the game. Remove any separate local installation to avoid duplicates.

Click the assignment icon at the lower left to run. Open the gear for settings. [b]Ctrl + Alt + O[/b] shows or hides the controls.

Automatic assignment is off by default. Minute timers include pauses; assignments wait until the simulation resumes. The start button stays locked while a request is active. Extra clicks do not restart or cancel it.

[b]Please note:[/b] paused and unsupported buildings retain their workers. The builder reserve and job requirements remain binding, so shortages can still leave buildings unstaffed. Keep a backup save.

[b]v0.2.1-hotfix.1:[/b] delayed confirmations can now recover automatically. If confirmation remains missing, the run shows a failed report instead of endless loading. The button stays locked until the outstanding command is confirmed or the world is reloaded; commands are never blindly resent. In-game acceptance of this hotfix is pending. Try a separate test save first.

